      "indexical_grounding_and_tie_breaking": "Colleague 4 introduced a very strong angle: 'The Global Coordinate Fallacy'. External logicians number seats 0 through 8, but an agent sitting in an unnumbered ring sees only an unlabelled sequence of 6 hats. While the necklace is asymmetric, off-axis seats (3, 4, 6, 7) do not possess internal chiral orientation relative to their blind spot without an absolute reference point.",
